  "native_linux_qualified": false,
  "public_api": {
    "added": [
      "xcronCalendarCursorInit",
      "xcronCalendarCursorInitCivil",
      "xcronCalendarCursorStep",
      "xcronCalendarCursorStepCivil"
    ],
    "cursor_bytes": 256,
    "cursor_alignment": 8,
    "existing_expression_bytes": 56,
    "existing_issue_bytes": 12,
    "pending_status": 2,
    "existing_values_and_layouts_preserved": true,
    "synchronous_apis_never_return_pending": true
  },
  "contracts": [
    "Init copies expression and bounds; only validation, rounding, constant ready-match and constant absence proof. No borrowed input, heap, clock, lock, worker or Unit duty.",
    "Cursor is address bound; reject byte relocation/copies, permit serialized same-address thread handoff and exclusive reinitialization.",
    "Positive Step month budget bounds additional visits; PENDING leaves Next unchanged, FOUND alone writes Next, terminal reads are repeatable; cumulative visits <=4801.",
    "Structural span/alias errors preserve all outputs; argument/state errors do not advance; failed Init preserves Cursor; typed diagnostics survive error-allocation OOM.",
    "Month/day absence proof preserves restricted DOM/DOW disjunction. MonthsExamined changes from4801 to0 for proven impossible February30 conjunction; NONE/result/ambient-error behavior is preserved."
  ],
  "costs": [
    "Public context occupies256 caller bytes. Init snapshots expression56 plus dates, clears output storage and encodes private state.",
    "Public Step decodes/encodes private state through memcpy, at most256 bytes each way, plus context/mode/span validation, bounded bitmap/date arithmetic and found-result conversion. Larger budgets amortize copies/calls.",
    "No new heap, runtime, thread, dependency or lock. Diagnostics may allocate on failure; normal results do not. No zero-overhead or wall-clock/OS scheduling guarantee.",
    "The old synchronous control loop remains specialized after shared cursor-state prototypes regressed common cases; bitmap/date rules and constant pruning are shared. This deliberate control-flow duplication is a maintenance cost."
  ],
  "regressions": [
    "All1500 independent brute earliest-match UTC oracles also run cursor queries with varied budgets; known cases use budget1.",
    "Independent146097-day Gregorian table checks5208 month/day/weekday conjunction/disjunction cases and validates actual found dates.",
    "Raw typed engine independently exhausts all4801 fallback months at budget1, bypassing only the analytic Init proof to retain cap coverage.",
    "UTC int64 millisecond and civil nonzero-int64-year endpoints, rounding, copied inputs, modes, aliases/wrapped spans, failed-init atomicity, terminal idempotence, handoff and diagnostic OOM.",
    "Sparse Sunday leap-day absence searches94 months over94 budget1 calls, preserving all pending outputs, ambient error and requested-allocation counters.",
    "Runnable calendar example uses budget16; external static/shared consumer executes all four new symbols."
  ],
